  ('37d96a01-0359-5d99-9834-29e023f0393a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The word "warp" often means "to bend or twist out of shape." In paragraph 2, what does "warp" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"the threads that are passed back and forth with a shuttle","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-part-whole"},{"text":"the long threads that run from top to bottom on a loom","is_correct":true},{"text":"the wooden frame that holds all of the threads","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"a thread that has bent out of its proper shape","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"common-meaning-instead"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$the long threads that run from top to bottom on a loom$q$, $q$Aunt Adaeze defines the warp as "these long threads that run from the top of the loom to the bottom," which "stay in place." Nkechi expects a thread to bend, but it is "stretched as straight as a guitar string," so the everyday meaning of bent does not fit here.$q$, 'draft', '5439b18a-a4f1-5547-9e26-ad34e22bc669')
